NAME
        bal asyncapi ws - Generate Ballerina source files from an AsyncAPI
                         definition for WebSocket protocol, or
                         generate an AsyncAPI definition from a
                         Ballerina service file

SYNOPSIS
        bal asyncapi ws -i <input-file-path>
                        [-o <output-directory>]
                        [--module <module-name>]
                        [--license <license-file-path>]
                        [--json]
                        [--service <service-name>]
                        [--with-tests]

DESCRIPTION
        The flow direction is determined automatically from the file
        extension of the --input argument:

        - .yaml, .yml, or .json  →  spec-to-code: generates Ballerina
          source files from an AsyncAPI definition for WebSocket
          protocol integrations.

        - .bal  →  code-to-spec: generates an AsyncAPI definition from
          a Ballerina service file. Use --service to target a specific 
          named service when the file contains multiple services. 
          Use --json to write the output definition in JSON format 
          instead of the default YAML.

        SPEC-TO-CODE OUTPUT:
        The output directory must be a Ballerina package. If a --module flag is provided, the
        generated files are written into the modules/<module-name>/
        directory of that package. If no --module flag is
        given, the generated files are written directly into the root of
        the package.

        CODE-TO-SPEC OUTPUT:
        The --output flag in code-to-spec mode specifies where the
        generated AsyncAPI spec file is written.

OPTIONS
        -i, --input <input-file-path>
                This is a mandatory input. The path to the AsyncAPI
                definition file (.yaml, .yml, or .json) for
                spec-to-code generation, or the path to the
                Ballerina service file (.bal) for code-to-spec
                generation.

        -o, --output <output-directory>
                This is an optional input. The path to the target
                output directory for the generated files.
                If not given, defaults to the current working directory.

        --module <module-name>
                This is an optional input. The name of the Ballerina
                module to generate code into. Only valid in spec-to-code

        --license <license-file-path>
                This is an optional input. The path to a file
                containing the license header to be added to all
                generated Ballerina files. Applicable only in
                spec-to-code mode.

        --json
                This is an optional input. If set, the generated
                AsyncAPI definition is written in JSON format
                instead of the default YAML format. Applicable
                only in code-to-spec mode.

        --service <service-name>
                This is an optional input. The name of a specific
                service in the Ballerina source file for which an
                AsyncAPI definition should be generated. Applicable
                only in code-to-spec mode (when a .bal file is
                given as input).

        --with-tests
                This is an optional input. If set, test files are
                generated alongside the service files. Applicable
                only in spec-to-code mode.

        -h, --help
                Display help for the ws subcommand.

EXAMPLES
        Generate Ballerina WebSocket files from an AsyncAPI definition
        in the current directory.

            $ bal asyncapi ws -i definition.yaml

        Generate Ballerina WebSocket files into a specific Ballerina
        package.

            $ bal asyncapi ws -i definition.yaml \
                              -o ./myproject

        Generate Ballerina WebSocket files into a specific module
        inside a Ballerina package.

            $ bal asyncapi ws -i definition.yaml \
                              --module payments

        Generate Ballerina WebSocket files and also generate test files.

            $ bal asyncapi ws -i definition.yaml \
                              -o ./myproject \
                              --with-tests

        Generate AsyncAPI definitions for all services in a Ballerina
        file.

            $ bal asyncapi ws -i service.bal

        Generate an AsyncAPI definition for a specific service in a
        Ballerina file.

            $ bal asyncapi ws -i service.bal \
                              --service ChatService

        Generate an AsyncAPI definition in JSON format.

            $ bal asyncapi ws -i service.bal \
                              --json
